__NAME__ - copy files to standard output

__NAME__ writes each file operand, or standard input, to standard output.


Requirements
------------
A C99 compiler and a POSIX make.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (__NAME__ is installed into the
/usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install __NAME__ (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running
-------
    __NAME__ [-v] [file...]

See __NAME__(1).


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of __NAME__ is done by editing config.h and (re)compiling
the source code. config.h is copied from config.def.h on the first build;
customisations are kept as patches against config.def.h.
